en, stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2(x+1)}.$\n\n![](images/c5/c52f568868328061237d43e4650180321ec4a40e886a62f4a678f0276afe821b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4e178c7-bdb4-5139-a20c-3e17de51ee11" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between Two Points With Variable Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b1c11b-b4b1-536c-8889-3a3eb09882dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}\\,w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395425} {:answer/id #uuid "c96ad5b8-0210-5052-9081-f410de18a5e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395426} {:answer/id #uuid "398a8fd3-2eed-529b-9541-d6be85bc82d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395427} {:answer/id #uuid "04663b1a-f275-5578-853a-d2e34a0425ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\,w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395428} {:answer/id #uuid "16d6cb4d-d2f4-501f-8ae8-ed5949dd56c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}\\,w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16d6cb4d-d2f4-501f-8ae8-ed5949dd56c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}\\,w" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395429} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea09eb90-beeb-5d00-94ad-88249fe8aeca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb9ffaa1-a202-507f-aa7e-4d95a973e5e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-98142" :question/problem "Calculate the distance between the points $(3w,2w,7w)$ and $(-w,6w,3w),$ given that $w$ is positive." :question/worked-solution "The distance $d$ between two points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1},{z}_{1})$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2},{z}_{2})$ is given by\n\n$$\nd=\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1}{)}^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1}{)}^{2}+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1}{)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have ${{(3w,2w,7w)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{, }{y}_{1}\\text{, }{z}_{1}\\text{)}}$ and ${{(-w,6w,3w)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{, }{y}_{2}\\text{, }{z}_{2}\\text{)}}.$ Applying the distance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(-w-3w{)}^{2}+(6w-2w{)}^{2}+(3w-7w{)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4w{)}^{2}+(4w{)}^{2}+(-4w{)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{w}^{2}+16{w}^{2}+16{w}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48{w}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48}\\,\\sqrt{{w}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{3}\\,|w|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $w$ is positive, we have $|w|=w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nd=4\\sqrt{3}\\,w.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea2f1348-55bf-5313-8d5e-a5a097231e97" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Stretched Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a4dc8da-0af6-521a-94e2-29efe502a4ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e2/e2a1274fc65341a659bb76923bb69677cc33bad1b78dfdf64ba97e0c8a00fb9c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068423} {:answer/id #uuid "b6cfcb00-3352-501b-8c96-ce26e77b5a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3a1cac41b2f9d6773226d76722508e6d7f368a42a0f7e86a5d8407d6f42c149.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068424} {:answer/id #uuid "23e003a0-4faa-5012-ab5b-6a16e4b56306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/79/79