x}.$\n\n![](images/34/344a3615421b88df05cb666ca90395991f3aa6af75c9095a60c73be89124b7e9.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4974097a-95c9-5835-ba1d-46480efab66b" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Limit at Infinity of a Power Function With an Even Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77040257-dfcd-57ee-adef-b30d8720c7f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361366} {:answer/id #uuid "9d480512-a430-5168-bbb8-6f7b524ac9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361541} {:answer/id #uuid "adc98796-c457-5bfd-aea7-8955623c63fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361604} {:answer/id #uuid "c65c7ecc-22dc-5be5-9e4e-a8fb9fd39891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361734} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b72881-45d9-5283-802c-9ab4aa1511b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77040257-dfcd-57ee-adef-b30d8720c7f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361366} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e92819f-13f4-5b8a-81f5-2ab190207cd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0160257-6d01-50d3-a643-02b7249aff4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-99275" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(8{x}^{12}).$" :question/worked-solution "The graph $y={x}^{12}$ looks similar to an upward parabola, so\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{12}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nMultiplication by the positive constant $8$ does not affect the limit at infinity. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(8{x}^{12})={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{12})=\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
